"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"planner","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"verification","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"lld-1c09e09c-s1-r1","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1","status":"changes_requested","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":3,"LOW":2},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The chosen approach addresses delayed task-count feedback and preserves existing contracts. However, it leaves the originating issue’s docs-band and attempt-budget decision unresolved. No diagram or UX artifact is necessary for this internal correction-message change; the prose contracts adequately describe its boundaries.","findings":[{"id":"scope-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/openQuestions/0; /body/alternativesConsidered/2; /body/alternativesConsidered/3","message":"The LLD defers part of the originating ISSUE’s fix intent without establishing that the retained policy supports a valid docs plan within three attempts. The ISSUE explicitly requires reviewing the XL band and attempt budget and setting them appropriately for the docs catalog. Instead, a3/a4 defer that assessment until another run fails, while openQuestions leaves whether it belongs in this Story undecided. The captured run proves delayed feedback and a persistent 15-task plan; it does not establish that 20 meaningful tasks are appropriate or reachable within the retained budget. The catalog supports repeated parameterized templates and child plans, so its small template count alone also cannot justify lowering the band. Resolve the scope decision and document a catalog-grounded justification for retaining or changing the band and budget, with explicit acceptance expectations. Additional model-call cost alone is insufficient grounds under the repository’s accuracy-first principle.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md: Fix intent and Root cause",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json: /body/alternativesConsidered/2/reasonRejected",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json: /body/alternativesConsidered/3/reasonRejected",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json: /body/openQuestions/0","src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts: docsFamilySummarise, docsDecisionTrace, docsConstraintEnumerate, docsSubrunDeepDive","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/01.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/02.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.plan.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md: Retry loop and XL → planner-template tasks","AGENTS.md instructions supplied in conversation: Accuracy is primary; cost is the least priority"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/3","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md","src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-br