andalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md: Reproduction and Fix intent","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/01.feedback.json: INV-7","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/02.feedback.json: INV-11","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.feedback.json: INV-13, 15 tasks versus focused XL minimum 20","src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts: DOCS_TEMPLATES","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts: retry loop and primary-feedback persistence"]},{"id":"verification-002","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/testStrategy/acceptanceMapping/0/criterionId","message":"The acceptance table maps every test to undefined criterion ac1; the originating ISSUE has no such identifier, and the LLD explicitly calls it a stand-in. Replace this placeholder with explicit expectations traced to the ISSUE's early-feedback and valid-docs-plan outcomes, so reviewers and builders can determine what each test proves.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json: /body/testStrategy/acceptanceMapping","docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/S001/LLD.md: sections 5 and 9","docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md: Fix intent"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/testStrategy","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/validate.test.ts","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/driver-unit.test.ts","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/wire-messages.test.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/private-paths.ts","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts","src/analyze/planner/cache.ts","src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts","src/analyze/connection-access.ts","design/analyze-plan-builder.md: Retry loop, focused intent, XL plans and persisted plan layout","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/01.plan.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/01.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/02.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.feedback.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["The live test asserts terminal success, a nonempty final report and partitioned handling. It can prove final-report delivery, but does not independently assert planner attempts, task counts or complete coverage; inspect the associated plan audit trail when using its result as planner evidence.","Include immediately outside each band boundary as well as exact endpoints. Existing fixture builders support this without live model calls.","Tests and live services were not executed during this read-only design assessment. No diagram or UX rendering is necessary for the assigned test-strategy change."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"passed","summary":"Whole-artifact consistency inspection found no additional defects beyond the accepted substantive feedback. All 20 inventory units received substantive inspection. Live and canonical documents match the checkpoint baseline and agree on the proposed behavior, acceptance mapping and unresolved questions. This chunk passes; the previously reported MED findings still block the overall design.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/lld-1c09e09c-s1-r1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:160-183,310-368,432-493,520-540","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:40-80,410-450","design/analyze-plan-builder.md: invariant policy, retry loop and focused lower bounds","checkpoint: completedChunks scope, planner and verification; inventory.units; plan.coverage; baseline.reviewedContent"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Retain scope-001, planner-001 and verification-001 as blocking findings: together they cover unresolved docs-policy feasibility, contradictory repetition semantics and insufficient reproduction coverage. No duplicate findings are added here.","Retain planner-002 and verification-002 for the incorrect runPlanner signature and undefined acceptance identifier.","The HLD-labelled metadata is present in both representations; standalone=true and the explicit no-parent-HLD statement establish the applicable ancestry. No Epic/HLD review is required.","No diagram or UX rendering is necessary for this internal correction-message change. Tests and live services were not executed during this read-only consistency assessment."]}],"limitations":[],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"0ced706f0982da825514eb8495bba8db81b4af0e34103bd61b585cd19a19cdf4"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-11T14:45:14.665Z"},{"number":2,"status":"changes_requested","preparationKind":"impact","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"143592f4d65e024fb92f649561f16abc2d865e69b9eac35ac713f071ebb3e362","document":"c3a5900f43f836a2b57d2d10fdecc89ce4d248adb957a24649c2e5b75e3d3fab"},"contentIdentity":"4f69005874db0f4da5d3aa392d32f2b470ab50d98a2979cb456c11df243ce85c","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"design.story\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794409263338-gnkuop\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-11T15:03:49.750Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-11T14:35:39.306Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-claude\",\n          \"model\": \"unknown\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 159195,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"1c09e09cd985026b\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before\",\n    \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n    \"hldBaseRunId\": \"wf-1794409263338-gnkuop\",\n    \"hldEffectiveHash\": \"abd56bbaf79579d7ad28dde52863648721224c4ac645d4498b3b699d06bfa88f\",\n    \"hldAmendmentsApplied\": [],\n    \"storyTitle\": \"Plan builder reports task-count errors early and fits the docs band (fix for ISSUE-1c09e09cd985026b)\",\n    \"standalone\": true,\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"lifecycle\": {\n      \"status\": \"draft\",\n      \"revision\": {\n        \"number\": 2,\n        \"contentHash\": \"552a212a5017e57496f3eb92b7a54f90abca2a2b13b0976becd598466f06f27b\",\n        \"at\": \"2026-11-11T15:03:51.597Z\",\n        \"by\": {\n          \"id\": \"insrc:system\",\n          \"kind\": \"system\",\n          \"properties\": {}\n        }\n      },\n      \"signoffs\": []\n    },\n    \"envelope\": {\n      \"attachments\": []\n    },\n    \"revision\": 2\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"prose\": \"The plan builder now tells the model about a wrong task count in the same correction turn as any other failure, shows the model the exact task-count range that the validator will enforce (no 'halve it' wording, one table for both), and allows more correction attempts for the plan than the shared retry setting does. The task-count band values, the invariant order, the failure type, the stored feedback files and the shared retry setting are unchanged; the reason the band is kept is written into the design and checked by the live regression.\",\n      \"audience\": \"technical\"\n    },\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"Plan builder reports task-count errors early and fits the docs band (fix for ISSUE-1c09e09cd985026b)\"\n      },\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {}\n    },\n    \"contractDetails\": {\n      \"surfaceLevel\": \"internal\",\n      \"api\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"validatePlan\",\n          \"signature\": \"validatePlan(plan: PlanTask, catalog: readonly AnalyzeTaskTemplate[], opts?: ValidateOpts): PlanValidationFailure | null\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"plan\",\n              \"type\": \"PlanTask\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The stamped plan to check\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"catalog\",\n              \"type\": \"readonly AnalyzeTaskTemplate[]\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Templates the plan may use\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"opts\",\n              \"type\": \"ValidateOpts\",\n              \"purpose\": \"focused / isChildPlan flags\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"PlanValidationFailure | null\",\n            \"meaning\": \"The first failing invariant, or null. Unchanged by this Story.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"plan has passed the wire-shape check\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Invariant order and the result for any plan are unchanged\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"appendCorrectionTurn\",\n          \"signature\": \"appendCorrectionTurn(prior: LLMMessage[], rejected: PlanTask, failure: PlanValidationFailure, priorFailures: readonly PlanValidationFailure[], alsoFailing?: PlanValidationFailure | undefined): LLMMessage[]\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"prior\",\n              \"type\": \"LLMMessage[]\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The conversation so far\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"rejected\",\n              \"type\": \"PlanTask\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The plan just rejected\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"failure\",\n              \"type\": \"PlanValidationFailure\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The first failing invariant; the primary message, and the only one the repetition banner compares\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"priorFailures\",\n              \"type\": \"readonly PlanValidationFailure[]\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Earlier primary failures, for the repetition banner\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"alsoFailing\",\n              \"type\": \"PlanValidationFailure | undefined\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The task-count failure (INV-13), stated after the primary one in the same turn\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"LLMMessage[]\",\n            \"meaning\": \"The conversation with the correction turn appended; with alsoFailing the turn names it after the primary failure and asks for both to be fixed\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"alsoFailing, when given, has invariantId INV-13 and failure does not\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Without alsoFailing the text is exactly what it is today\",\n            \"The repetition banner is decided by failure and priorFailures only; alsoFailing never enters failures[] or the banner\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"renderDepthPolicy\",\n          \"signature\": \"renderDepthPolicy(scope: 'XS' | 'S' | 'M' | 'L' | 'XL', focused: boolean): string\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"scope\",\n              \"type\": \"'XS' | 'S' | 'M' | 'L' | 'XL'\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The plan's size\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"focused\",\n              \"type\": \"boolean\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Whether the intent is focused\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"meaning\": \"The depth-policy block of the planner prompt. It states the one range that validatePlan enforces for this scope and focus, taken from the same table, and no longer says that a focused intent 'reduces the lower bound to half'.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"The range printed is the range INV-13 checks, for every scope and both focus values\",\n            \"No band table is kept in the renderer\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"runPlanner\",\n          \"signature\": \"runPlanner(args: RunPlannerArgs): Promise<PlanTask>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"args\",\n              \"type\": \"RunPlannerArgs\",\n              \"purpose\": \"{ input: PlanBuilderInput; opts: PlanBuilderOpts; provider?: LLMProvider | undefined }\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"PlanTask\",\n            \"meaning\": \"The accepted plan. Unchanged.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"PlanBuilderExhausted\",\n              \"condition\": \"No attempt passed all invariants within the planner's attempt limit; carries the primary failures\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"The correction loop runs up to the planner's own attempt limit (a named constant in the planner, 5: the first reply plus four corrections) instead of cfg.shaper.structuredOutputRetries\",\n            \"The wire-level maxAttempts given to completeStructured, and every other user of cfg.shaper.structuredOutputRetries, are unchanged\",\n            \"When the first failure is not INV-13 and the count is outside the band, the correction turn also states the count failure\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dataModelChanges\": [\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"SCOPE_BAND\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"Values unchanged (XS 3-8, S 10-20, M 20-40, L 30-60, XL 40-80; focused lower bound halved). The table and the focused lower bound move to a leaf module in the planner that imports nothing from the validator or the renderer, so both can import it and the duplicate in the renderer is deleted. Retention reason, from the docs catalog and the run: the six docs templates take parameters, so 20 or more meaningful tasks are reachable (inventory, one summary per family, one deep-dive per area, decision.trace and constraint.enumerate where the question needs them, aggregator); the failed run is explained by a misread range (its own reasoning says 10-80) and a count error shown only on the last attempt. Revisit trigger: a live run in which the model was told the count and the exact range and still cannot produce a valid plan.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:61\",\n          \"src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:163\",\n          \"src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts:79\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"PlanValidationFailure\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"No field change. The task-count check is exposed as a function returning a PlanValidationFailure for INV-13 or null, with the same band, lower bound and message as the check inside validatePlan, which calls it at its INV-13 position; the retry loop calls it for the secondary note.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:40\",\n          \"src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:418\",\n          \"src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:325\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"interactionWithShared\": [],\n    \"errorPaths\": {\n      \"errorCases\": [\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A plan fails an ordering invariant and also has a task count outside the band\",\n          \"detection\": \"After validatePlan returns a failure whose invariantId is not INV-13, the retry loop runs the task-count check on the same stamped plan and gets a non-null INV-13 failure\",\n          \"response\": \"The correction turn states the primary failure first and the count failure second and asks for both to be fixed; failures[] and feedback.json record only the primary failure\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"None visible; the run needs fewer attempts\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The count was a secondary note on one attempt and is the primary failure on the next\",\n          \"detection\": \"validatePlan returns INV-13 as the first failure while the last entry of failures[] is a different invariant\",\n          \"response\": \"No repetition banner, because the banner compares primary failures only and the count was never recorded as one; the correction turn is the same as today's for an INV-13 failure\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"None\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"No attempt in the planner's limit passes every invariant\",\n          \"detection\": \"The loop ends after the planner's attempt limit with failures.length equal to the limit\",\n          \"response\": \"PlanBuilderExhausted with the primary failures, as today; the run fails with plan-invariant-failed\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The run fails at the plan stage as today, after at most four corrections instead of two\",\n          \"recoverable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The range shown to the model and the range validated differ\",\n          \"detection\": \"Both come from one table in a leaf module; a unit test compares the printed range with the INV-13 band for every scope and both focus values\",\n          \"response\": \"Fails in tests; nothing to handle at run time\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"None\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"edgeCases\": [\n        {\n          \"input\": \"The first failure is INV-13 itself\",\n          \"expected\": \"No also-failing section; the turn text is identical to today's\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"The first failure is INV-1 (empty task list)\",\n          \"expected\": \"The count failure is also stated (0 tasks is outside every band) and the primary failure stays INV-1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A focused plan at XL\",\n          \"expected\": \"The depth policy prints 20-80 once, without wording about halving, and INV-13 checks 20-80\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A child plan with a smaller scope\",\n          \"expected\": \"The count check and the printed range use the plan's own scope band, as validatePlan does\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"The count is inside the band\",\n          \"expected\": \"No also-failing section; turn text identical to today's\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Planner limit and the shared retry setting differ\",\n          \"expected\": \"The loop uses the planner limit; completeStructured still receives the shared setting as its own maxAttempts\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"invariantsToPreserve\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"validatePlan returns the first failing invariant in numeric order, and its result for any plan is unchanged\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"failures[], feedback.json, PlanBuilderExhausted and the orchestrator error carry primary failures only, one per attempt, and the repetition banner compares only those\",\n          \"source\": \"c2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"cfg.shaper.structuredOutputRetries keeps its value and its other users (classifier, aggregator, adherence runtime, wire-level schema repair)\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"SCOPE_BAND values and the halved focused lower bound are unchanged\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The plan is stamped with the intent's scope before validation, so the model cannot choose its own band\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"testStrategy\": {\n      \"testLevels\": [\n        {\n          \"level\": \"unit\",\n          \"purpose\": \"ac1 (count stated beside the primary failure, with banner and history rules kept) and ac2 (the range shown is the range enforced, from one table)\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"task-count check against validatePlan INV-13 at the lower and upper bound of XS..XL, focused and not\",\n            \"appendCorrectionTurn without alsoFailing is byte-identical to today's; with alsoFailing the primary comes first and the count second\",\n            \"repetition banner: a count that was a secondary note and then becomes the primary failure gets no banner; a primary INV-13 repeated on the next attempt still gets one\",\n            \"renderDepthPolicy prints for every scope and both focus values the same range as the INV-13 band, once, with no 'half' wording\",\n            \"no band table remains in render-catalog.ts, and the table module imports nothing from the validator or the renderer\",\n            \"validatePlan order and results unchanged for the existing invariant cases\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"PlanTask builders used by validate.test.ts\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"ac3 on the production retry loop: the reproduced sequence is recovered inside the planner's limit, using the docs catalog and scripted replies through structuredStageForTest\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"reply 1: 15 docs tasks, INV-7 plus count: the correction turn states INV-7 first and the count second\",\n            \"reply 2: 20 or more docs tasks, INV-11 still present: the correction turn names INV-11 only, with no count section and no banner\",\n            \"reply 3: a valid in-band docs plan is accepted at attempt 3; failures[] and feedback.json hold INV-7 and INV-11 only\",\n            \"a scripted run that needs all five attempts is accepted on the fifth, and one that never passes throws PlanBuilderExhausted with five primary failures\",\n            \"completeStructured still receives the shared structuredOutputRetries value as its own maxAttempts\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"registered docs templates (src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts)\",\n            \"structuredStageForTest scripted replies\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"live\",\n          \"purpose\": \"ac3 on a real model: the broad docs request runs to a final report\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts with INSRC_LIVE_TESTS=1; a failure after the count and the exact range were shown triggers the band revisit written into the design\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac1\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"validate.test.ts: the task-count check agrees with validatePlan at every band boundary\",\n            \"driver-unit.test.ts: appendCorrectionTurn states the count after the primary failure and is unchanged without it\",\n            \"driver-unit.test.ts: repetition banner follows primary failures only, including the secondary-to-primary transition\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac2\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"driver-unit.test.ts: renderDepthPolicy prints the INV-13 range for every scope and focus value, without halving wording\",\n            \"driver-unit.test.ts: no duplicate band table in the renderer\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac3\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"driver-unit.test.ts: scripted docs-catalog replay (INV-7 plus count, INV-11, valid) accepted at attempt 3 with primary-only feedback\",\n            \"driver-unit.test.ts: five-attempt acceptance and exhaustion with the planner limit\",\n            \"docs-broad-live.test.ts: broad docs request reaches a final report (live)\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"testFramework\": \"node:test via tsx (npx tsx --test), assert/strict, as in the existing planner tests\"\n    },\n    \"migration\": {\n      \"stateBefore\": \"validatePlan reports only the first failing invariant, so the task count (INV-13) shows only after INV-7, INV-11 and INV-12 are cleared (src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:418). renderDepthPolicy keeps a second copy of the band table and tells a focused plan that the lower bound is 'reduced to half' next to a number that is already halved (src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts:79), and the failed run's plan reasoned about a 10-80 band. The retry loop allows cfg.shaper.structuredOutputRetries attempts, 3 by default, one correction turn per failure (src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:241).\",\n      \"stateAfter\": \"The first failure stays the primary message and the same correction turn also states the task-count failure when the count is outside the band. The prompt prints the exact range that INV-13 enforces from the one table, without halving wording. The correction loop has its own named attempt limit of 5. SCOPE_BAND values, invariant order, PlanValidationFailure, stored feedback files and the shared retry setting are unchanged.\",\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"action\": \"Move the band table and the focused lower bound into a leaf planner module; make validatePlan and the renderer import it, with no change to any value\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"action\": \"Rewrite the depth-policy text to print the enforced range once, without the halving wording, and delete the renderer's copy of the table\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 3,\n          \"action\": \"Expose the task-count check as a function that validatePlan calls at its existing INV-13 position, with no change to its result\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 4,\n          \"action\": \"Extend the correction-turn builder to accept an optional count failure rendered after the primary failure; with none given the text is unchanged\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 5,\n          \"action\": \"In the retry loop, when the first failure is not INV-13, run the count check on the same plan and pass a non-null result to the correction-turn builder; keep primary-only history, feedback and banner\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 6,\n          \"action\": \"Give the correction loop its own named attempt limit of 5 and keep the shared setting for the wire-level call and every other user\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"No public API, wire shape, stored file shape or config key changes. The observable changes are the wording of the depth-policy block and of the correction message in the planner prompt, and up to four corrections instead of two before a plan fails. Persisted feedback.json files and PlanBuilderExhausted keep the same fields; PlanBuilderExhausted can now carry up to five failures. Anything that read the attempt count as the shared setting must read the planner limit.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": true,\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": false\n    },\n    \"alternativesConsidered\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"name\": \"Count check ahead of the ordering checks\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Return the task-count failure first so a wrong count is told to the model in attempt 1.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Move the INV-13 check so validatePlan evaluates the task-count band before the ordering invariants (INV-7, INV-11, INV-12), keeping one failure per attempt. A plan with a wrong count and an ordering error is told about the count first; the ordering error comes once the count is right.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Smallest edit to validatePlan; no new types and the repetition banner keeps its meaning\",\n          \"A count error is the largest, cheapest correction\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Still one invariant per attempt, so a plan with a wrong count and two ordering errors uses three attempts\",\n          \"Reorders the documented invariant order, which tests and the design doc rely on\",\n          \"Does nothing about the misleading band text that made the model believe 15 tasks was in band\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"S\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Moves which error is hidden instead of removing the hiding, reorders documented invariants, and ignores two of the three causes in the run.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"name\": \"Count as a secondary note on the correction turn\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Keep the first failure as primary and state the count problem in the same turn, without entering the failure history.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Expose the task-count check as its own function, called by validatePlan at its INV-13 position and by the retry loop when the first failure is something else. appendCorrectionTurn gets an optional second failure rendered after the primary one. failures[], feedback files and the repetition banner keep primary-only semantics: the banner compares only primary failures, so a count that was a secondary note and then becomes primary does not trigger a banner.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Fixes the observed hiding without changing invariant order, PlanValidationFailure or stored files\",\n          \"The count check is a pure function and easy to test\",\n          \"Turns without a second failure are byte-identical to today's\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Alone it does not make the model understand the band: the 10-80 miscalculation would repeat\",\n          \"Leaves the attempt budget at the shared value of 3, so the reproduced sequence (INV-7 plus count, then INV-11, then valid) only just fits\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Right fix for the hidden count but leaves the cause of the wrong count in the first place, and no slack in the budget.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a3\",\n        \"name\": \"Secondary note, one exact band, and a planner attempt budget\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"a2, plus the band stated to the model exactly as it is validated, plus a planner-specific attempt limit; band values stay as they are.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Do a2. In addition: (1) the depth-policy text takes its numbers from the same table the validator uses and states the final range once, without the 'reduces the lower bound to half' wording that the model applied a second time (10-80 in its own reasoning); the duplicated table is removed so the two cannot drift. (2) The planner's correction loop gets its own attempt limit, a named constant in the planner, used for the loop only; the shared structuredOutputRetries stays the budget of the classifier, aggregator, adherence runtime and the wire-level schema repair. SCOPE_BAND values are retained, with the catalog-based reason recorded: the docs catalog has six templates that take parameters, so a plan of 20 or more meaningful tasks is reachable (inventory, one summary per family, one deep-dive per area, decision.trace and constraint.enumerate where the question asks for them, aggregator), and the one observed failure is explained by the misread band and the hidden count error.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Addresses each cause shown by the run: the hidden count, the misread band, and the tight budget\",\n          \"No change to the invariant order, failure type, stored files or shared retry setting\",\n          \"A single band table removes the drift risk found in render-catalog.ts\",\n          \"The band decision is documented with evidence and a stated trigger for revisiting it\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"More work than a2 and touches the prompt text, so behaviour on live models must be confirmed by the live regression\",\n          \"A larger planner budget can mean more model calls for a plan that cannot be fixed\",\n          \"Retaining the band relies on one run plus catalog reading; a later live failure after the count is told would reopen it\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a4\",\n        \"name\": \"Change the XL band for docs plans\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Give plans built from the docs catalog a lower task-count band.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Replace the single band lookup with one that depends on the template family, so docs plans are held to a floor the docs catalog supports, while code families keep 40-80 (20 focused).\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Removes any mismatch between the floor and a small catalog\",\n          \"Code families unchanged\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Rewrites a policy shared by all families on the evidence of one run in which the model misread the band\",\n          \"A lower floor weakens the plan-size check and must be justified by the catalog; the catalog supports 20 or more parameterised tasks\",\n          \"Needs per-family data in the validator and the prompt\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Changes shared policy to fit one observation that has a simpler explanation; the catalog supports 20 or more parameterised tasks. Revisit only if a live run that was told the count and the exact band still cannot reach the floor.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"chosenAlternative\": \"a3\",\n    \"openQuestions\": [\n      \"The Story has no formal acceptance criteria: ac1-ac3 are expectations derived from the ISSUE's fix intent (early count feedback, a band shown as validated, a recoverable reproduced sequence with a documented band and budget decision). A reviewer should confirm they reflect the ISSUE.\",\n      \"invariantsToPreserve cite c1..c3, which map to the code citations in References (validate.ts:418, driver.ts:524, driver.ts:241); the s1 bundles carry no ids of their own.\",\n      \"The planner attempt limit of 5 gives the reproduced sequence two attempts of slack; it is not measured. The live regression and the stated band revisit trigger cover it.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:418\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"INV-13: scope policy adherence -- task count within the band.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:524\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"function repetitionBannerFor(\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:241\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"const maxAttempts = cfg.shaper.structuredOutputRetries;\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts:79\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"export function renderDepthPolicy(scope: 'XS' | 'S' | 'M' | 'L' | 'XL', focused: boolean): string {\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"step-output\",\n      \"ref\": \"~/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.plan.json\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"use 15 tasks, within its focused 10–80 band\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1 -->\n\n# LLD: STORY-1c09e09cd985026b-s1 — Plan builder reports task-count errors early and fits the docs band (fix for ISSUE-1c09e09cd985026b)\n\n## Summary\n\n**Epic:** `plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before`\n**HLD base run:** `wf-1794409263338-gnkuop`\n**HLD effective hash:** `abd56bbaf795...`\n\nThe plan builder now tells the model about a wrong task count in the same correction turn as any other failure, shows the model the exact task-count range that the validator will enforce (no 'halve it' wording, one table for both), and allows more correction attempts for the plan than the shared retry setting does. The task-count band values, the invariant order, the failure type, the stored feedback files and the shared retry setting are unchanged; the reason the band is kept is written into the design and checked by the live regression.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [HLD context](#1-hld-context)\n2. [Contract details](#2-contract-details)\n3. [Data model changes](#3-data-model-changes)\n4. [Error paths](#4-error-paths)\n5. [Test strategy](#5-test-strategy)\n6. [Migration](#6-migration)\n7. [Alternatives considered](#7-alternatives-considered)\n8. [References](#8-references)\n9. [Open questions](#9-open-questions)\n\n## 1. HLD context\n\n**Framework:** Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\n**Rollout phase:** standalone\n\n## 2. Contract details\n\n**Surface level:** internal\n\n### 2.1 `validatePlan`\n\n```typescript\nvalidatePlan(plan: PlanTask, catalog: readonly AnalyzeTaskTemplate[], opts?: ValidateOpts): PlanValidationFailure | null\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `plan: PlanTask` — The stamped plan to check\n- `catalog: readonly AnalyzeTaskTemplate[]` — Templates the plan may use\n- `opts: ValidateOpts` _(optional)_ — focused / isChildPlan flags\n\n**Returns:** `PlanValidationFailure | null` — The first failing invariant, or null. Unchanged by this Story.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- plan has passed the wire-shape check\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Invariant order and the result for any plan are unchanged\n\n### 2.2 `appendCorrectionTurn`\n\n```typescript\nappendCorrectionTurn(prior: LLMMessage[], rejected: PlanTask, failure: PlanValidationFailure, priorFailures: readonly PlanValidationFailure[], alsoFailing?: PlanValidationFailure | undefined): LLMMessage[]\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `prior: LLMMessage[]` — The conversation so far\n- `rejected: PlanTask` — The plan just rejected\n- `failure: PlanValidationFailure` — The first failing invariant; the primary message, and the only one the repetition banner compares\n- `priorFailures: readonly PlanValidationFailure[]` — Earlier primary failures, for the repetition banner\n- `alsoFailing: PlanValidationFailure | undefined` _(optional)_ — The task-count failure (INV-13), stated after the primary one in the same turn\n\n**Returns:** `LLMMessage[]` — The conversation with the correction turn appended; with alsoFailing the turn names it after the primary failure and asks for both to be fixed\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- alsoFailing, when given, has invariantId INV-13 and failure does not\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Without alsoFailing the text is exactly what it is today\n- The repetition banner is decided by failure and priorFailures only; alsoFailing never enters failures[] or the banner\n\n### 2.3 `renderDepthPolicy`\n\n```typescript\nrenderDepthPolicy(scope: 'XS' | 'S' | 'M' | 'L' | 'XL', focused: boolean): string\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `scope: 'XS' | 'S' | 'M' | 'L' | 'XL'` — The plan's size\n- `focused: boolean` — Whether the intent is focused\n\n**Returns:** `string` — The depth-policy block of the planner prompt. It states the one range that validatePlan enforces for this scope and focus, taken from the same table, and no longer says that a focused intent 'reduces the lower bound to half'.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The range printed is the range INV-13 checks, for every scope and both focus values\n- No band table is kept in the renderer\n\n### 2.4 `runPlanner`\n\n```typescript\nrunPlanner(args: RunPlannerArgs): Promise<PlanTask>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `args: RunPlannerArgs` — { input: PlanBuilderInput; opts: PlanBuilderOpts; provider?: LLMProvider | undefined }\n\n**Returns:** `PlanTask` — The accepted plan. Unchanged.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `PlanBuilderExhausted` when No attempt passed all invariants within the planner's attempt limit; carries the primary failures\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The correction loop runs up to the planner's own attempt limit (a named constant in the planner, 5: the first reply plus four corrections) instead of cfg.shaper.structuredOutputRetries\n- The wire-level maxAttempts given to completeStructured, and every other user of cfg.shaper.structuredOutputRetries, are unchanged\n- When the first failure is not INV-13 and the count is outside the band, the correction turn also states the count failure\n\n## 3. Data model changes\n\n### 3.1 `SCOPE_BAND` — invariant-change\n\nValues unchanged (XS 3-8, S 10-20, M 20-40, L 30-60, XL 40-80; focused lower bound halved). The table and the focused lower bound move to a leaf module in the planner that imports nothing from the validator or the renderer, so both can import it and the duplicate in the renderer is deleted. Retention reason, from the docs catalog and the run: the six docs templates take parameters, so 20 or more meaningful tasks are reachable (inventory, one summary per family, one deep-dive per area, decision.trace and constraint.enumerate where the question needs them, aggregator); the failed run is explained by a misread range (its own reasoning says 10-80) and a count error shown only on the last attempt. Revisit trigger: a live run in which the model was told the count and the exact range and still cannot produce a valid plan.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:61`\n- `src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:163`\n- `src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts:79`\n\n### 3.2 `PlanValidationFailure` — invariant-change\n\nNo field change. The task-count check is exposed as a function returning a PlanValidationFailure for INV-13 or null, with the same band, lower bound and message as the check inside validatePlan, which calls it at its INV-13 position; the retry loop calls it for the secondary note.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:40`\n- `src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:418`\n- `src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:325`\n\n## 4. Error paths\n\n**Error cases**\n\n- **A plan fails an ordering invariant and also has a task count outside the band** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: After validatePlan returns a failure whose invariantId is not INV-13, the retry loop runs the task-count check on the same stamped plan and gets a non-null INV-13 failure\n  - Response: The correction turn states the primary failure first and the count failure second and asks for both to be fixed; failures[] and feedback.json record only the primary failure\n  - User impact: None visible; the run needs fewer attempts\n- **The count was a secondary note on one attempt and is the primary failure on the next** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: validatePlan returns INV-13 as the first failure while the last entry of failures[] is a different invariant\n  - Response: No repetition banner, because the banner compares primary failures only and the count was never recorded as one; the correction turn is the same as today's for an INV-13 failure\n  - User impact: None\n- **No attempt in the planner's limit passes every invariant** (terminal)\n  - Detection: The loop ends after the planner's attempt limit with failures.length equal to the limit\n  - Response: PlanBuilderExhausted with the primary failures, as today; the run fails with plan-invariant-failed\n  - User impact: The run fails at the plan stage as today, after at most four corrections instead of two\n- **The range shown to the model and the range validated differ** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: Both come from one table in a leaf module; a unit test compares the printed range with the INV-13 band for every scope and both focus values\n  - Response: Fails in tests; nothing to handle at run time\n  - User impact: None\n\n**Edge cases**\n\n| Input | Expected |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| The first failure is INV-13 itself | No also-failing section; the turn text is identical to today's |\n| The first failure is INV-1 (empty task list) | The count failure is also stated (0 tasks is outside every band) and the primary failure stays INV-1 |\n| A focused plan at XL | The depth policy prints 20-80 once, without wording about halving, and INV-13 checks 20-80 |\n| A child plan with a smaller scope | The count check and the printed range use the plan's own scope band, as validatePlan does |\n| The count is inside the band | No also-failing section; turn text identical to today's |\n| Planner limit and the shared retry setting differ | The loop uses the planner limit; completeStructured still receives the shared setting as its own maxAttempts |\n\n**Invariants to preserve**\n\n- validatePlan returns the first failing invariant in numeric order, and its result for any plan is unchanged [[c1]]\n- failures[], feedback.json, PlanBuilderExhausted and the orchestrator error carry primary failures only, one per attempt, and the repetition banner compares only those [[c2]]\n- cfg.shaper.structuredOutputRetries keeps its value and its other users (classifier, aggregator, adherence runtime, wire-level schema repair) [[c3]]\n- SCOPE_BAND values and the halved focused lower bound are unchanged [[c1]]\n- The plan is stamped with the intent's scope before validation, so the model cannot choose its own band [[c3]]\n\n## 5. Test strategy\n\n**Test framework:** `node:test via tsx (npx tsx --test), assert/strict, as in the existing planner tests`\n\n**Test levels**\n\n- **unit** — ac1 (count stated beside the primary failure, with banner and history rules kept) and ac2 (the range shown is the range enforced, from one table)\n  - Subjects: `task-count check against validatePlan INV-13 at the lower and upper bound of XS..XL, focused and not`, `appendCorrectionTurn without alsoFailing is byte-identical to today's; with alsoFailing the primary comes first and the count second`, `repetition banner: a count that was a secondary note and then becomes the primary failure gets no banner; a primary INV-13 repeated on the next attempt still gets one`, `renderDepthPolicy prints for every scope and both focus values the same range as the INV-13 band, once, with no 'half' wording`, `no band table remains in render-catalog.ts, and the table module imports nothing from the validator or the renderer`, `validatePlan order and results unchanged for the existing invariant cases`\n  - Fixtures: `PlanTask builders used by validate.test.ts`\n- **integration** — ac3 on the production retry loop: the reproduced sequence is recovered inside the planner's limit, using the docs catalog and scripted replies through structuredStageForTest\n  - Subjects: `reply 1: 15 docs tasks, INV-7 plus count: the correction turn states INV-7 first and the count second`, `reply 2: 20 or more docs tasks, INV-11 still present: the correction turn names INV-11 only, with no count section and no banner`, `reply 3: a valid in-band docs plan is accepted at attempt 3; failures[] and feedback.json hold INV-7 and INV-11 only`, `a scripted run that needs all five attempts is accepted on the fifth, and one that never passes throws PlanBuilderExhausted with five primary failures`, `completeStructured still receives the shared structuredOutputRetries value as its own maxAttempts`\n  - Fixtures: `registered docs templates (src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts)`, `structuredStageForTest scripted replies`\n- **live** — ac3 on a real model: the broad docs request runs to a final report\n  - Subjects: `src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts with INSRC_LIVE_TESTS=1; a failure after the count and the exact range were shown triggers the band revisit written into the design`\n\n**Acceptance mapping**\n\n| Criterion | Proving tests |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `ac1` | `validate.test.ts: the task-count check agrees with validatePlan at every band boundary`, `driver-unit.test.ts: appendCorrectionTurn states the count after the primary failure and is unchanged without it`, `driver-unit.test.ts: repetition banner follows primary failures only, including the secondary-to-primary transition` |\n| `ac2` | `driver-unit.test.ts: renderDepthPolicy prints the INV-13 range for every scope and focus value, without halving wording`, `driver-unit.test.ts: no duplicate band table in the renderer` |\n| `ac3` | `driver-unit.test.ts: scripted docs-catalog replay (INV-7 plus count, INV-11, valid) accepted at attempt 3 with primary-only feedback`, `driver-unit.test.ts: five-attempt acceptance and exhaustion with the planner limit`, `docs-broad-live.test.ts: broad docs request reaches a final report (live)` |\n\n## 6. Migration\n\n**State before:** validatePlan reports only the first failing invariant, so the task count (INV-13) shows only after INV-7, INV-11 and INV-12 are cleared (src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:418). renderDepthPolicy keeps a second copy of the band table and tells a focused plan that the lower bound is 'reduced to half' next to a number that is already halved (src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts:79), and the failed run's plan reasoned about a 10-80 band. The retry loop allows cfg.shaper.structuredOutputRetries attempts, 3 by default, one correction turn per failure (src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:241).\n\n**State after:** The first failure stays the primary message and the same correction turn also states the task-count failure when the count is outside the band. The prompt prints the exact range that INV-13 enforces from the one table, without halving wording. The correction loop has its own named attempt limit of 5. SCOPE_BAND values, invariant order, PlanValidationFailure, stored feedback files and the shared retry setting are unchanged.\n\n**Zero downtime:** yes — **Data rewrite:** no\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Move the band table and the focused lower bound into a leaf planner module; make validatePlan and the renderer import it, with no change to any value — ↩ rollbackable\n2. Rewrite the depth-policy text to print the enforced range once, without the halving wording, and delete the renderer's copy of the table — ↩ rollbackable\n3. Expose the task-count check as a function that validatePlan calls at its existing INV-13 position, with no change to its result — ↩ rollbackable\n4. Extend the correction-turn builder to accept an optional count failure rendered after the primary failure; with none given the text is unchanged — ↩ rollbackable\n5. In the retry loop, when the first failure is not INV-13, run the count check on the same plan and pass a non-null result to the correction-turn builder; keep primary-only history, feedback and banner — ↩ rollbackable\n6. Give the correction loop its own named attempt limit of 5 and keep the shared setting for the wire-level call and every other user — ↩ rollbackable\n\n**Backward compat:** No public API, wire shape, stored file shape or config key changes. The observable changes are the wording of the depth-policy block and of the correction message in the planner prompt, and up to four corrections instead of two before a plan fails. Persisted feedback.json files and PlanBuilderExhausted keep the same fields; PlanBuilderExhausted can now carry up to five failures. Anything that read the attempt count as the shared setting must read the planner limit.\n\n## 7. Alternatives considered\n\n### 7.1 a1: Count check ahead of the ordering checks\n\nReturn the task-count failure first so a wrong count is told to the model in attempt 1.\n\nMove the INV-13 check so validatePlan evaluates the task-count band before the ordering invariants (INV-7, INV-11, INV-12), keeping one failure per attempt. A plan with a wrong count and an ordering error is told about the count first; the ordering error comes once the count is right.\n\n**Rejected because:** Moves which error is hidden instead of removing the hiding, reorders documented invariants, and ignores two of the three causes in the run.\n\n### 7.2 a2: Count as a secondary note on the correction turn\n\nKeep the first failure as primary and state the count problem in the same turn, without entering the failure history.\n\nExpose the task-count check as its own function, called by validatePlan at its INV-13 position and by the retry loop when the first failure is something else. appendCorrectionTurn gets an optional second failure rendered after the primary one. failures[], feedback files and the repetition banner keep primary-only semantics: the banner compares only primary failures, so a count that was a secondary note and then becomes primary does not trigger a banner.\n\n**Rejected because:** Right fix for the hidden count but leaves the cause of the wrong count in the first place, and no slack in the budget.\n\n### 7.3 a3: Secondary note, one exact band, and a planner attempt budget — **CHOSEN**\n\na2, plus the band stated to the model exactly as it is validated, plus a planner-specific attempt limit; band values stay as they are.\n\nDo a2. In addition: (1) the depth-policy text takes its numbers from the same table the validator uses and states the final range once, without the 'reduces the lower bound to half' wording that the model applied a second time (10-80 in its own reasoning); the duplicated table is removed so the two cannot drift. (2) The planner's correction loop gets its own attempt limit, a named constant in the planner, used for the loop only; the shared structuredOutputRetries stays the budget of the classifier, aggregator, adherence runtime and the wire-level schema repair. SCOPE_BAND values are retained, with the catalog-based reason recorded: the docs catalog has six templates that take parameters, so a plan of 20 or more meaningful tasks is reachable (inventory, one summary per family, one deep-dive per area, decision.trace and constraint.enumerate where the question asks for them, aggregator), and the one observed failure is explained by the misread band and the hidden count error.\n\n### 7.4 a4: Change the XL band for docs plans\n\nGive plans built from the docs catalog a lower task-count band.\n\nReplace the single band lookup with one that depends on the template family, so docs plans are held to a floor the docs catalog supports, while code families keep 40-80 (20 focused).\n\n**Rejected because:** Changes shared policy to fit one observation that has a simpler explanation; the catalog supports 20 or more parameterised tasks. Revisit only if a live run that was told the count and the exact band still cannot reach the floor.\n\n## 8. References\n\n- **[[c1]]** `code` `src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:418` — \"INV-13: scope policy adherence -- task count within the band.\"\n- **[[c2]]** `code` `src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:524` — \"function repetitionBannerFor(\"\n- **[[c3]]** `code` `src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:241` — \"const maxAttempts = cfg.shaper.structuredOutputRetries;\"\n- **[[c4]]** `code` `src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts:79` — \"export function renderDepthPolicy(scope: 'XS' | 'S' | 'M' | 'L' | 'XL', focused: boolean): string {\"\n- **[[c5]]** `step-output` `~/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.plan.json` — \"use 15 tasks, within its focused 10–80 band\"\n\n## 9. Open questions\n\n- The Story has no formal acceptance criteria: ac1-ac3 are expectations derived from the ISSUE's fix intent (early count feedback, a band shown as validated, a recoverable reproduced sequence with a documented band and budget decision). A reviewer should confirm they reflect the ISSUE.\n- invariantsToPreserve cite c1..c3, which map to the code citations in References (validate.ts:418, driver.ts:524, driver.ts:241); the s1 bundles carry no ids of their own.\n- The planner attempt limit of 5 gives the reproduced sequence two attempts of slack; it is not measured. The live regression and the stated band revisit trigger cover it.\n"},"capturedAt":"2026-11-11T15:03:59.659Z"},"inventory":{"units":[{"id":"/body/summary","selector":"/body/summary","title":"summary","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/hldContextSlice","selector":"/body/hldContextSlice","title":"hldContextSlice","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/contractDetails","selector":"/body/contractDetails","title":"contractDetails","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/dataModelChanges","selector":"/body/dataModelChanges","title":"dataModelChanges","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/interactionWithShared","selector":"/body/interactionWithShared","title":"interactionWithShared","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/errorPaths","selector":"/body/errorPaths","title":"errorPaths","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/testStrategy","selector":"/body/testStrategy","title":"testStrategy","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/migration","selector":"/body/migration","title":"migration","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered","title":"alternativesConsidered","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/chosenAlternative","selector":"/body/chosenAlternative","title":"chosenAlternative","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/openQuestions","selector":"/body/openQuestions","title":"openQuestions","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","title":"a1","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","title":"a2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","title":"a3","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/3","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/3","title":"a4","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/citations/0","selector":"/citations/0","title":"Citation 1","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/1","selector":"/citations/1","title":"Citation 2","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/2","selector":"/citations/2","title":"Citation 3","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/3","selector":"/citations/3","title":"Citation 4","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/4","selector":"/citations/4","title":"Citation 5","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:25","selector":"document:line:25","title":"1. HLD context","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The proposed combined fix addresses the originating ISSUE: concurrent count feedback, an exact shared band policy, and a separate five-attempt planner budget. Retaining the bands is reasonably grounded in parameterized docs templates, with live validation and a revisit trigger explicitly required. Acceptance expectations match the issue's fix intent. The internal import and correction-flow changes are adequately described in prose; no additional diagram or UX rendering is necessary.","findings":[{"id":"scope-r1-002","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2/approach; LLD.md:234","message":"The design states that the model applied the halving wording a second time as an established cause. The cited renderer contains potentially ambiguous wording, and the captured plan demonstrably uses 10–80, but its reasoning does not attribute that range to a second halving. Describe double-halving as a plausible explanation rather than a demonstrated cause, including the corresponding assertions in the alternatives.","evidenceReferences":["src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts:79-102","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.plan.json:reasoning","/body/alternativesConsidered/0/cons","/body/alternativesConsidered/1/cons","/body/alternativesConsidered/2/approach"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/3","/citations/4","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:1-165","docs/plans/docs-module.md:123-130","docs/plans/docs-module.md:260-270","src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts","src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:225-365","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:418-434","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.plan.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Treat five attempts as the explicitly acknowledged policy choice pending live evidence. Live execution was not performed during this read-only design review.","When implementing the new budget, update the upstream planner design's three-attempt retry description to keep the documented policy aligned."]},{"chunkId":"planner","status":"passed","summary":"All assigned sections and citations were inspected against the originating ISSUE and current planner code. The design preserves invariant ordering, stamped scope ownership, focused rounding, child-plan behavior and primary-only failure history. Shared band extraction is feasible, five-attempt histories fit existing persistence and error contracts, and the planner budget remains separate from wire-level repair. The internal interactions are adequately described in prose; no additional diagram or UX rendering is necessary.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/lld-1c09e09c-s1-r1.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:178-373 — RunPlannerArgs, sequential calls, separate wire budget, scope stamping and primary failure ownership","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:395-478 — initial prompt and correction composition","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:524-559 — repetition compares the immediately preceding primary failure and target identity","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:40-68 — failure shape and exported scope bands","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:163-180 — focused floor rounding and validation options","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:183-482 — invariant ordering and INV-13 message","src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts:69-104 — duplicated bands and current focused wording","src/analyze/planner/cache.ts — unrestricted attempt numbering and primary feedback serialization","src/analyze/planner/types.ts — input, scope, parent-path and error contracts","src/analyze/planner/recursive.ts:150-204 — measured child scope, sequential recursion and child error ownership","src/analyze/planner/index.ts:40-46 — SCOPE_BAND re-export","src/analyze/index.ts:48 — upstream SCOPE_BAND export","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:840-861 — exhaustion maps to last primary failure and actual attempt count","src/config/analyze.ts:186-192 — shared retry default","src/analyze/classifier/driver.ts:170 — shared wire retry consumer","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/aggregator.ts:140 — shared retry consumer","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/adherence.ts:297 — shared retry consumer","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/driver-unit.test.ts:125-154 — existing renderer assertions","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/recursive.test.ts:490-499 — existing three-reply exhaustion fixture"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Preserve the existing SCOPE_BAND exports when moving ownership to the leaf module, including consumers importing through validate.ts and the planner barrel.","Update existing three-reply exhaustion fixtures and assertions for the old focused wording alongside implementation. Keep the upstream planner design's retry description aligned with the separate budgets.","No tests or live provider calls were executed during this read-only design review."]},{"chunkId":"verification","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The revised acceptance mapping and regression sequence align with the ISSUE and combined fix. However, the selected scripted test hook cannot verify the promised correction messages or provider retry budget without additional instrumentation.","findings":[{"id":"verification-003","severity":"MED","location":"/body/testStrategy/testLevels/1; LLD.md:179-181","message":"The integration strategy promises correction-message and completeStructured maxAttempts assertions through structuredStageForTest, but that hook receives neither messages nor provider options. With the hook enabled, runPlanner skips initial-message construction and bypasses completeStructured entirely. It exercises validation, failure history and saved-mode persistence, but cannot prove that production calls receive the secondary count feedback or preserve the shared wire budget. Specify an observation hook exposing the actual messages and options, or a provider stub that traverses the normal message/provider branch. Separate helper tests do not verify the driver's wiring.","evidenceReferences":["src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:171-181 — PlannerStructuredTestArgs and structuredStageForTest","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:218-235 — fixture mode skips prompt/provider and initial messages","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:269-286 — scripted stage bypasses completeStructured and its options","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:374 — correction messages are retained locally","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/wire-messages.test.ts: calls helper captures actual provider messages","docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/S001/LLD.md:179-181"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/testStrategy","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts","src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts","src/analyze/planner/cache.ts","src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/driver-unit.test.ts","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/validate.test.ts","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/wire-messages.test.ts","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/wire-decode.test.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/private-paths.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts: classifyPlannerError","design/analyze-plan-builder.md: Retry loop, focused intents and XL child plans","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/01.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/02.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/01.plan.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/02.plan.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.plan.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make the boundary matrix explicit: lo-1, lo, hi and hi+1 for every scope/focus combination, plus a child whose own scope differs from rootScope. Existing focused and child tests do not establish that complete matrix. Use meaningful parameterized docs tasks rather than repeated padding in the valid in-band fixture.","The live regression was source-inspected, not executed. Its assertions establish a successful partitioned final report; its saved record does not establish the exercised band, count-feedback delivery or complete coverage. When running it, retain planner audit evidence and distinguish count-related planner exhaustion from downstream failures before invoking the band-revisit trigger. No relevant authored or generated visual accompanies the assigned test strategy."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"passed","summary":"Fresh consistency inspection found no additional defects. Current live and canonical documents agree, all 21 inventory units received substantive inspection, and the combined fix addresses the ISSUE's scope. Earlier findings are reconciled below. The overall review remains blocked by the current verification-003 MED finding.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-befo