persistence and exhaustion checks are feasible. The live test can establish final-report delivery, but the deterministic regression does not cover the observed multi-error sequence or demonstrate acceptance using the docs catalog.","findings":[{"id":"verification-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/testStrategy/testLevels/1","message":"The only successful retry scenario jumps from INV-7 plus 15 tasks directly to acceptance on reply 2. It omits the subsequent INV-11 failure that consumed another attempt in the originating ISSUE, and specifies only a registered catalog rather than a representative docs plan. Consequently, it does not establish the claimed recovery within the existing three-attempt budget for the reproduced case. Add a deterministic docs-catalog regression that exposes count feedback alongside INV-7, retains the independently failing INV-11 after the first correction, and reaches a valid in-band plan on the final allowed attempt. Assert the correction messages, attempt count and primary-only feedback across that sequence.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/S001/LLD.md: section 5, integration subjects and fixtures","docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md: Reproduction and Fix intent","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/01.feedback.json: INV-7","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/02.feedback.json: INV-11","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.feedback.json: INV-13, 15 tasks versus focused XL minimum 20","src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts: DOCS_TEMPLATES","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts: retry loop and primary-feedback persistence"]},{"id":"verification-002","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/testStrategy/acceptanceMapping/0/criterionId","message":"The acceptance table maps every test to undefined criterion ac1; the originating ISSUE has no such ide