or extraction and correction-loop integration","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2"],"concerns":["Inspect actual validator and driver code to assess helper inputs, focused and child-plan semantics, invariant ordering and stamped scope.","Assess correction-message composition, secondary-failure eligibility, repetition handling and unchanged behavior when no secondary failure exists.","Verify primary-failure ownership across retry history, exhaustion errors and persisted feedback.","Check implementation order, rollback feasibility, compatibility claims, citations and applicable TypeScript and provider conventions.","Inspect any necessary authored or generated interaction artifacts and actual renderings where available."],"dependsOn":["scope"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"verification","title":"Regression coverage and acceptance evidence","selectors":["/body/testStrategy"],"concerns":["Check acceptance mapping against the originating ISSUE rather than an assumed story acceptance criterion.","Inspect referenced test files and fixtures for feasible boundary, correction-message, retry, persistence and exhaustion coverage.","Assess whether the proposed integration regression represents the observed sequence of ordering failures and the docs task-count constraint.","Distinguish mandatory evidence inspection from optional live execution; assess whether the live test can establish the claimed final-report outcome."],"dependsOn":["scope","planner"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Whole-artifact consistency and upstream alignment","selectors":[],"concerns":["Check missing ISSUE requirements, cross-chunk contradictions and shared contracts across scope, implementation and verification.","Reconcile live-document and canonical-artifact content, including metadata, acceptance claims and unresolved questions.","Confirm every inventory unit received substantive inspection and consolidate evidence, limitations and findings under the required status precedence."],"dependsOn":["scope","planner","verification"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 20 inventory units map to substantive chunks. Scope and policy decisions precede validator and driver integration, followed by verification of those responsibilities. The final consistency chunk depends on every substantive chunk and checks whole-artifact alignment without replacing unit coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["planner"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["planner"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["planner"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["planner"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["verification"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["planner"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/3","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["planner"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["planner"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["planner"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"document:line:25","chunkIds":["scope"]}]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"planning","phase":"planning","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"planner","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"verification","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"lld-1c09e09c-s1-r1","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1","status":"changes_requested","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":3,"LOW":2},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The chosen approach addresses delayed task-count feedback and preserves existing contracts. However, it leaves the originating issue’s docs-band and attempt-budget decision unresolved. No diagram or UX artifact is necessary for this internal correction-message change; the prose contracts adequately describe its boundaries.","findings":[{"id":"scope-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/openQuestions/0; /body/alternativesConsidered/2; /body/alternativesConsidered/3","message":"The LLD defers part of the originating ISSUE’s fix intent without establishing that the retained policy supports a valid docs plan within three attempts. The ISSUE explicitly requires reviewing the XL band and attempt budget and setting them appropriately for the docs catalog. Instead, a3/a4 defer that assessment until another run fails, while openQuestions leaves whether it belongs in this Story undecided. The captured run proves delayed feedback and a persistent 15-task plan; it does not establish that 20 meaningful tasks are appropriate or reachable within the retained budget. The catalog supports repeated parameterized templates and child plans, so its small template count alone also cannot justify lowering the band. Resolve the scope decision and document a catalog-grounded justification for retaining or changing the band and budget, with explicit acceptance expectations. Additional model-call cost alone is insufficient grounds under the repository’s accuracy-first principle.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md: Fix intent and Root cause",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json: /body/alternativesConsidered/2/reasonRejected",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json: /body/alternativesConsidered/3/reasonRejected",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json: /body/openQuestions/0","src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts: docsFamilySummarise, docsDecisionTrace, docsConstraintEnumerate, docsSubrunDeepDive","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/01.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/02.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.feedback.json","/home/subho/.insrc/analyze/docs-broad-live-mwc5fz8p/plan.attempts/03.plan.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md: Retry loop and XL → planner-template tasks","AGENTS.md instructions supplied in conversation: Accuracy is primary; cost is the least priority"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/3","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-1c09e09cd985026b-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/plan-builder-runs-out-attempts-before-E202611111c09e09c/ISSUE.md","src/analyze/planner/templates/docs/index.ts","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.te